  "parent": {
    "number": 37,
    "title": "Add YCbCr (PI=6) support to TiffExporter",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nYCbCr (PhotometricInterpretation=6) images are currently unsupported. The test suite includes 5 YCbCr images, only one of which (`dscf0013.tif`) is uncompressed. Supporting YCbCr requires a new exporter class that upsamples the chroma channels (Cb/Cr) and converts to RGB, since subsampled YCbCr cannot fit the library's flat N-channels-per-pixel model.\n\n## Context\n\n- YCbCr images in the test suite: `dscf0013.tif` (uncompressed, 2×1 subsampling), `quad-jpeg.tif` (JPEG), `smallliz.tif` (Old JPEG), `ycbcr-cat.tif` (LZW), `zackthecat.tif` (Old JPEG, tiled).\n- Only `dscf0013.tif` can be supported without also adding compression support.\n- The `Image` struct and `copyRectangles` machinery already support N channels and planar config; no structural changes needed.\n\n## Requested changes\n\n1. **Add YCbCr tags to the `Tag` enum**: `YCbCrCoefficients = 0x0211`, `YCbCrSubsampling = 0x0212`, `YCbCrPositioning = 0x0213`, `ReferenceBlackWhite = 0x0214`.\n\n2. **Add `TiffExporterYCbCr` class** (modeled on `TiffExporterRgb`):\n   - `requireSamplesPerPixel(ifd, 3)`, `requirePhotometricInterpretation(ifd, 6)`.\n   - Read `YCbCrSubsampling` (default 1,1), `YCbCrPositioning` (default 1), `YCbCrCoefficients` (default 0.299/0.587/0.114), `ReferenceBlackWhite` (default per TIFF spec).\n   - Upsample Cb/Cr channels to full resolution (nearest-neighbor or better).\n   - Convert each pixel from YCbCr to RGB using the coefficients and reference levels.\n   - `Image::make<DstType, 3>(width, height)` for the output.\n\n3. **Dispatch in `TiffExporterAny`**: add `photometricInterpretation == 6` branch (chunky only is acceptable initially).\n\n4. **Handle planar configuration** if feasible (chunky is sufficient for the existing test images).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `dscf0013.tif` (uncompressed YCbCr, 2×1 subsampling) is exported correctly as RGB.\n- The exported image dimensions and channel count match the source.\n- `TiffCraft::load()` with `TiffExporterAny` succeeds on `dscf0013.tif` without throwing.\n- Existing tests continue to pass.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Compression support (JPEG, LZW, Old JPEG) — separate concern.\n- Planar (separate) YCbCr — can be added later if needed.",
