  body: "Follow-up on the YCbCr fixture set: I removed `ycbcr-16bit-1x1.tif` and its ground-truth PPM (commit `45cb5bf`), dropped the case from `tests/ycbcr_images/generate_ycbcr.py`, removed its matrix row from `tests/YCBCR_SUPPORT.md`, and corrected the image count from 18 to 17 in the changelog.\n\nWhy: TIFF 6.0 Class Y (YCbCr) and libtiff define `BitsPerSample = <8,8,8>` — libtiff's own coverage docs list that for YCbCr, and its RGBA conversion path only initialises YCbCr conversion for 8-bit data. Our spec reference already states `BitsPerSample = 8, 8, 8` in two places. The 16-bit case was therefore nonstandard, and ImageMagick forces the YCbCr conversion back to 8-bit, so the committed file did not actually have 16-bit samples despite its name and documentation row. Rather than force a mislabeled/nonstandard fixture into the set, I removed it. The remaining 17 fixtures are all produced by running `tests/ycbcr_images/generate_ycbcr.py`.",
