      "body": "## Review — #39 (issue #38): YCbCr test coverage\n\nCI: Ubuntu/Consumers/MacOS success; Windows still in progress. Mergeable blocked (likely pending Windows or a rebase check).\n\n### Findings (docs accuracy)\n\nThe YCBCR_SUPPORT.md document has three factual errors in the spec reference:\n\n1. **ReferenceBlackWhite default wrong** (line 19): table says `(0, 255, 0, 128, 0, 128)`, should be `(0, 255, 128, 255, 128, 255)` per TIFF spec and Pillow output. Notes repeat the error.\n2. **YCbCrSubsampling default wrong** (line 17): says `1, 1` but spec default is `2, 2`.\n3. **Reverse B formula has extra term** (line 46): `B = Y + 1.772 * (Cb - 128) - 0.081312 * (Cr - 128)` should be `B = Y + 1.772 * (Cb - 128)`.\n\n### Everything else checks out\n- Tag codes, types, counts: correct\n- Forward conversion formulas: correct\n- Subsampling factors (1, 2, 4): correct\n- Positioning (1=centered, 2=cosited): correct\n- Minimum requirements: correct\n- Test image matrix: accurate\n- Generator script and test data: present and auditable\n\n### Verdict\nNo code changes; no functional blockers. Three doc-accuracy fixes needed before merge.",
